    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d555">

                <pb facs="0931" n="884" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v03mSupp/pg884"/>

                <head>555. Telegram 1707 from Geneva<anchor n="1" xml:id="d555-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Geneva</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1956-03-29">March 29, 1956, 4
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d555-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d555-1"/>
                <p>1707. From Johnson.</p>
                <p>Comments today’s meeting:</p>
                <p>Believe Wang considers that his shift today from former take it or leave it
                    attitude with respect his October 27 and December 1 drafts was move on their
                    part to get talks off dead center, and that next move is up to us. Do not
                    believe he will submit any new draft next meeting. However I feel his move today
                    gives us opportunity present new draft without same disadvantages as heretofore,
                    if we desire do so.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Gowen</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
